. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.universalDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.universalDeriv","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The universal derivation `d : A → Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.differentials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.differentials","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The object of Kähler differentials `Ω¹(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean#L31-L56","doc":"**Spatial realization functor**.\n\nGiven a quantum observable universe `(C, A, τ)`, the spatial realization\n`Spec(A)` is the collection of categorical points `p : 𝟙 → A`.  The\nfibre functor `τ : C → D` maps the algebraic structures on `A` —\nKähler differentials `Ω¹(A)`, the Frobenius-induced contact form `θ_A`,\nand the Reeb derivation `ξ` — to their geometric counterparts on the\nmanifold `M = τ(Spec(A))`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:spatial-realization-functor}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:spatial-realization-functor","label":"def:spatial-realization-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}